{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_spec", "label": "VLM Image Validation + Label-Order Fix Design", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two independent defects fixed together purely because they share the image-upload code path (routes/api_routes.py \u2192 services/image/)."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_vlm_validation_gate", "label": "GPT-4o Vision Lesion Validation Gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Problem 1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without it, faces/objects/scenery get a confident but meaningless skin-cancer label. The legacy Flask app had this gate in utils/validation.py and it was lost in the FastAPI rewrite. Uses AsyncOpenAI natively (no asyncio.to_thread), base64 data URL from in-memory bytes with no temp file, temperature=0 and ~10 max_tokens, and the prompt is ported verbatim from the legacy module."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_validation_unavailable_error", "label": "ValidationUnavailableError (Fail-Closed Signal)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Problem 1 / Error-handling summary", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Any SDK/network/timeout error or empty API key raises this and maps to 503 with no classification \u2014 fail closed. Deliberately asymmetric with the 'uncertain' verdict, which fails OPEN and lets the image through, on the grounds that a parsing hiccup should not reject a real lesion."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_label_order_fix", "label": "SKIN_CANCER_LABELS Order Fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Problem 2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The FastAPI rewrite put Melanoma at index 0, but the trained skinCancer.h5 emits classes in the legacy order, so argmax index 0 (really Karsinoma Sel Basal) was reported as Melanoma; only Nevus at index 3 stayed correct. Preprocessing was explicitly ruled out as the cause \u2014 legacy img_to_array and current np.array both feed raw 0-255 RGB at 224x224 with normalization baked into the model \u2014 so preprocessing is left unchanged. Fixed in both hardcoding sites (classifier + schemas/detection.py Literal), which an existing test already asserts stay in sync."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_local_decode_precheck", "label": "Cheap Local Decode Pre-Check", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Wiring", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Image.open(...).verify() runs before the VLM call so corrupt or non-image bytes are rejected locally with a 400 without spending an OpenAI request. Needed because validation now runs ahead of the classifier, which previously produced that 400."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_validation_status_field", "label": "validation_status Response Field", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Schema", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Literal['valid','uncertain'] because only those two verdicts can reach a 200. Exposed specifically so the UI can surface an 'uncertain' advisory rather than presenting a borderline classification as confident."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_bilingual_rejection_message", "label": "Bilingual Image Rejection Message", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Wiring", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Indonesian primary, English secondary, matching the UI-chrome-is-Indonesian convention while staying legible to English speakers."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_spec", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_vlm_validation_gate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Problem 1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_spec", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_label_order_fix", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Problem 2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_vlm_validation_gate", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_validation_unavailable_error", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Problem 1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_local_decode_precheck", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_vlm_validation_gate", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Wiring", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_vlm_validation_gate", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_validation_status_field", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Schema", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_vlm_validation_gate", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_bilingual_rejection_message", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "Wiring", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_vlm_validation_gate", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_20_skin_cancer_rag_design_module_boundary_rule", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-05-vlm-image-validation-and-label-fix-design.md", "source_location": "New component", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_05_vlm_image_validation_and_label_fix_design_label_or